There were 39 girls and 4 boys trying out for the basketball team. First, we calculate the total number of students who tried out:

$$
39 \text{ girls} + 4 \text{ boys} = 43 \text{ students}
$$

Next, we subtract the number of students who got called back (26) from the total number of students:

$$
43 - 26 = 17
$$

Thus, the number of students who didn't make the cut is $\boxed{17}$.  
