Mike is tasked with putting away books at the library. The total number of books is 82, but a librarian takes 10 of them, leaving Mike with $ 82 - 10 = 72 $ books to put away.

Each shelf can hold 9 books. To determine how many shelves Mike needs, we divide the number of books he has left by the number of books per shelf:

$$
72 \div 9 = 8
$$

Since this division is exact (no remainder), Mike will need exactly 8 shelves to hold all 72 books. Therefore, the answer is:

$$
\boxed{8}
$$

