 money did Victor make in those two days?

To determine how much money Victor made in those two days, we start by calculating his earnings for each day individually. 

On Monday, Victor worked for 5 hours at a rate of $6 per hour. This means his earnings for Monday are $ 5 \text{ hours} \times 6 \text{ dollars/hour} $.

Similarly, on Tuesday, Victor also worked for 5 hours at the same rate, so his earnings for Tuesday are also $ 5 \text{ hours} \times 6 \text{ dollars/hour} $.

We then add the earnings for both days to get the total. The total earnings can be calculated as $ (5 \times 6) + (5 \times 6) $.

Simplifying this expression, we get $ 30 + 30 = 60 $.

Therefore, the total amount of money Victor made in those two days is \boxed{60}. 

