Wendy initially picked 103 flowers. After 47 of them wilted, the number of remaining flowers is calculated as follows:

$$
103 - 47 = 56
$$

She is making bouquets with 8 flowers each. To determine how many bouquets she can make, divide the remaining flowers by the number of flowers per bouquet:

$$
56 \div 8 = 7
$$

Thus, the number of bouquets she can still make is:

$$
\boxed{7}
$$

