To determine how many more problems the teacher has to grade, we first calculate the total number of problems across all worksheets. 

- Each worksheet contains 7 problems.
- The teacher has 17 worksheets to grade.

$$
\text{Total problems} = 17 \text{ worksheets} \times 7 \text{ problems per worksheet} = 119 \text{ problems}
$$

Next, we calculate the number of problems the teacher has already graded. 

- She has already graded 8 worksheets.

$$
\text{Problems graded} = 8 \text{ worksheets} \times 7 \text{ problems per worksheet} = 56 \text{ problems}
$$

To find the remaining number of problems to grade:

$$
\text{Remaining problems} = 119 \text{ total problems} - 56 \text{ graded problems} = 63 \text{ problems}
$$

Thus, the teacher has to grade $\boxed{63}$ more problems. 

