Now, moving on to the caramel candy. He has 5 boxes, each with 4 pieces. So that would be 5 boxes multiplied by 4 pieces per box. Let me calculate that: 5 * 4. Hmm, 5 times 4 is 20. So that's 20 pieces of caramel candy. 

