\text{Next, calculate the number of problems for reading homework:}
4 \text{ pages} \times 5 \text{ problems/page} = 20 \text{ problems}

\text{Add the problems together:}
10 \text{ problems} + 20 \text{ problems} = 30 \text{ problems}

\text{Alternatively, sum the pages first and then multiply by problems per page:}
(2 \text{ pages} + 4 \text{ pages}) \times 5 \text{ problems/page} = 6 \times 5 = 30 \text{ problems}

\text{Both methods confirm the total number of problems is } \boxed{30}.
