Now, the problem says that Oliver can fit 4 books on a shelf. I need to find out how many shelves he will need. To do this, I should divide the number of books by the number of books per shelf. So that would be 36 divided by 4. Let me calculate that. 

36 divided by 4 is 9. Wait, is that right? Let me check. 4 times 9 is 36, yes. So that means Oliver needs 9 shelves. 

